        "original_id": "ad11a14d-2a68-5a96-8e6c-933df3cbfb64",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Fincke, Scott Kelly, Gennady Padalka, André Kuipers\n- Roles: Astronauts, International Space Station commanders\n- Places: International Space Station, Russia, USA, Netherlands\n- Missions: Soyuz TMA-4, Expeditions 26, 45, 46\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Fincke was born on March 14, 1967, and is an American astronaut.\n- Michael Fincke formerly held the American record for the most time in space with 381.6 days.\n- Soyuz TMA-4 flew Gennady Padalka of Russia, Michael Fincke of the USA, and André Kuipers of the Netherlands to the International Space Station.\n- Scott Kelly was a veteran of four space flights and commanded the International Space Station on Expeditions 26, 45, and 46.\n- Scott Kelly broke Michael Fincke's American record for the most time in space on October 16, 2015.",
